<h1>Work & Responsibilities</h1>

<p>
Hi folks, I am an aging millenial whose biggest fear in life is being called a "poser" by my younger self. 	
</p>

<p>
I have an unhealthy obsession with all technologies, including police surveillance. I am an expert on police surveillance and my work has been covered extensively. My tips and primary source documents into Clearview AI because the basis for <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20200630164223/https://www.nytimes.com/2020/01/20/reader-center/insider-clearview-ai.html">The New York Times front-page coverage</a> of the company and lead to international outrage, including millions of dollars of fines levied against the company and lawsuits all over the world.
As retaliation, the company attempted to <a href="https://www.politico.com/news/2021/09/24/clearview-ai-subpoena-watchdog-groups-514273">subpoena me multiple times to reveal my records and sources.</a> 
</p>

<p>
Of course, a large part of my work is focused on Chicago and has been covered by places like the <a href="https://chicago.suntimes.com/crime/2026/08/27/flock-license-plate-reader-alpr-chicago-suburb">Chicago Sun-Times</a>. My original writings can be found in places like <a href="https://www.404media.co/facial-recognition-company-clearview-attempted-to-buy-social-security-numbers-and-mugshots-for-its-database/">404Media</a>, <a href="https://truthout.org/articles/ice-kidnapped-my-neighbor-in-broad-daylight-the-aftermath-left-me-reeling/">Truthout</a>, and <a href="https://www.thenation.com/article/politics/doj-trump-espionage-act/">The Nation</a> among others. 
It also means I often talk to politicians, local organizers, criminal defense attorneys, members of the public, classrooms, or at conferences.
</p>

<p>
<b>If you want to retain me as an expert witness about police surveillance technologies under Rule 26 or on the local level, get in touch.</b>
</p>
<p>
I am a co-founder and staff worker at the Lucy Parsons Labs which we established over 11 years ago. I have also worked on government transparency issues, classification reform, the Freedom of Information Act, and other projects. I previously was a software and security engineer and studied physics. 
</p>

